get.description:
Server-Sent Events stream of live run state — the same feed the StagingPro UI uses for its progress bar.

The stream emits a `state` event immediately, another on every engine update, and a single `end` event when the run reaches a terminal status. A run that has already finished — or whose engine-side working files have since been reclaimed — receives `end` straight away, so the stream always closes cleanly; read finished runs from `GET /migrations/{id}` (the durable store) instead of re-opening the stream. Comment pings keep the connection alive.

```js
const es = new EventSource('/v2/api/bc-migration/migrations/' + id + '/stream');
es.addEventListener('state', (e) => render(JSON.parse(e.data)));
es.addEventListener('end', () => es.close());
```

text/event-stream.example:
event: state
data: {"requestId":"5A3C…","status":"in_progress","progress":{"phase":"products","percent":42}}

event: end
data: {}
